From c464ff604228d8369701b276b95cf69bf53375ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:35:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] script: carry an iframe's browsing context name into other
 script threads

The iframe `name` attribute is stored on the WindowProxy in the parent's
script thread. When the iframe navigates to a host served by another script
thread, that thread creates a fresh WindowProxy with an empty name, so the
child's window.name was "". Dailymotion's player passes its configuration
through the iframe name; without it the player never initialised, the page's
player promise never resolved, and the React app never mounted (blank page).

Send the name with IFrameLoadInfo, forward it through the constellation in
NewPipelineInfo, and apply it when the loading script thread creates the
WindowProxy for the browsing context.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 components/constellation/constellation.rs              | 8 ++++++++
 components/script/dom/html/htmliframeelement.rs        | 4 ++++
 components/script/dom/window/windowproxy.rs            | 1 +
 components/script/navigation.rs                        | 3 +++
 components/script/script_thread.rs                     | 9 +++++++++
 components/shared/constellation/from_script_message.rs | 4 ++++
 components/shared/script/lib.rs                        | 4 ++++
 7 files changed, 33 insertions(+)

